Text:
fearlessOnClick is a program that the desk runs when a person opens a file, for example with a double click, and that fearlessManager runs with the one argument "Reconcile".
fearlessOnClick turns the path that the desk gives into a Base16, and runs fearlessMessage.
fearlessOnClick sends only Messages that any other program can send.
//later: what a person sees when fearlessMessage prints on its standard error
//later: what a person sees after a "Register " Base16 that is applied
//later: fearlessOnClick remembers the extensions that the person did not let fearlessOnClick take

Grammar:
FearlessExtension ::= "fearless" | "fapp" [0-9][0-9][0-9] | "ffile" [0-9][0-9][0-9]

Story:
A event fearlessOnClick starts with the one argument "Reconcile".
B action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage with the one argument "Extensions"
C fact fearlessMessage prints "Applied\n" OSExtension1 "\n" .. OSExtensionn "\n"
D fact OSExtensions holds exactly OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn and every text of form FearlessExtension.
E fact TaggedText encodes the path of the currently running fearlessOnClick.
F action reconciliator$reconcile(TaggedText,OSExtensions)

Story:
A event The desk opens a file with fearlessOnClick.
B fact The name of that file is of form ProjectName ".fearless", and Base16 encodes the path of the folder that holds that file.
C action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage with the one argument "Register " Base16

Story:
A event The desk opens a file with fearlessOnClick.
B fact The name of that file is not of form ProjectName ".fearless", and Base16 encodes the path of that file.
C action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage with the one argument "Openers " Base16
D fact fearlessMessage prints "Applied\n" Message "\n"
E action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage with the one argument Message

Story:
A event The desk opens a file with fearlessOnClick.
B fact The name of that file is not of form ProjectName ".fearless", and Base16 encodes the path of that file.
C action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage with the one argument "Openers " Base16
D fact fearlessMessage prints "Applied\n" Message0 "\n" Message1 "\n" Message2 "\n" .. Messagen "\n"
E action fearlessOnClick shows Message0 .. Messagen in a dialog
F event The person picks Messagei in that dialog.
G action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage with the one argument Messagei

Story:
A event The desk opens a file with fearlessOnClick.
B fact The name of that file is not of form ProjectName ".fearless", and Base16 encodes the path of that file.
C action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage with the one argument "Openers " Base16
D fact fearlessMessage prints "Applied\n"
E action fearlessOnClick shows in a dialog that no main opens that file

Story:
A action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage with the one argument Message
B fact fearlessMessage prints "Refused\n" Error
C action fearlessOnClick shows Error in a dialog

Implementation notes:
On macOS the desk hands the files to open to fearlessOnClick in an open event; on the other desks the desk runs fearlessOnClick with the absolute path of each file as an argument.
When the desk opens several files at once, the Story happens once for each file.
